+/*
+ * kirin, boot-arg sweetmodem=1: bring up the SDM630 modem (MSS, the Hexagon Q6 that runs
+ * the cellular and Wi-Fi firmware), stage A. Unlike the ADSP (a simple TrustZone PAS), the
+ * modem self-authenticates through its MBA (Modem Boot Authenticator), as Linux's
+ * pil-q6v5-mss / pil-msa / pil-q6v5 for DT /soc/qcom,mss@4080000 (qcom,pil-q6v55-mss,
+ * qdsp6v62-1-5):
+ *
+ *   GCC clocks    MSS cfg_ahb, q6_bimc_axi, snoc_axi, mnoc_bimc_axi, boot_rom (0x100000)
+ *   reset         MSS_RESTART (GCC 0x179000): assert (1), then deassert (0)
+ *   MBA           mba.bin loaded into the MBA region (0x94800000); its address written to
+ *                 RMB_MBA_IMAGE (rmb_base 0x4180000 + 0x00)
+ *   Q6 out of     the QDSP6SS register dance (reg_base 0x4080000): XO clock, BHS head switch,
+ *   reset         LDO bypass, memory clamps and power, core out of reset, core clock
+ *   handshake     poll RMB_PBL_STATUS == 1 (the PBL validated the MBA), then RMB_MBA_STATUS
+ *
+ * Stage A stops once the MBA runs (PBL success). Loading modem.mdt and its segments through
+ * the RMB protocol, SMP2P, rmtfs, QMI are the later stages (research/modem-notes.md). No RPM
+ * rail votes yet: the bootloader left vdd_cx/vdd_mx on; if the PBL never validates, add them.
+ */
